{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat","id":1534297,"title":"Eachothers Throat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-16T09:49:23-07:00","id":1534297,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Eachothers Throat","content":"It's a general question I had while reviewing what one tribe thinks of the other, although most of it is somewhat predictable, I also came across a few surprises, like how the Sylent Striders tribebook portrays the CoG. Anyway, what I wanted to know is how the relationship between one tribe and another interferes outside the pack in practice for you?<br /> <br /> How is the relationship between one tribe and another? Do they respect each other? Are they tolerated? Do they distrust each other? Does this count for anything in the chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T12:44:03-07:00","id":1534300,"title":"","content":"I tend to treat the Garou tribes and septs like the ancient Greek city states or other Bronze Age warrior cultures. They have a common identity and culture (the Garou Nation), but feud and argue frequently with each other when not faced with an immediate threat. There are limited resources (kinfolk, friendly spirits, lost cubs, caern power, fetishes, prestige, etc.) that can justify a lot of competition, raids, or conflicts.<br /> <br /> In terms of politics, it's really the individual septs that decide things. A mono-tribal sept may decide to go to war against a different mono-tribal sept (or ally with, or be a vassal or overlord to, or any other political act). Tribes are too unwieldy to be commanded that way so there are no tribe versus tribe wars. Tribes can be at war in one place in the world, and further on out they can be close allies in another region. I tend to make lots of mono-tribal septs with low ranking caerns, and only the larger caerns be combinations of several tribes. So in the chronicle, you can see how tribal opinions play out. <br /> <br /> In my chronicles, septs like the Sept of the Green (the Central Park caern) that are open to any tribe are extremely rare. But I understand many games are based on large septs that include everyone (especially online or LARP) because that allows everyone to create whatever character they want. That keeps things fun, but I don't the setting is actually like that. <br /> <br /> If I do want multi-tribal packs and the like, I use the Anruth concept a lot. A lot of young Garou pack with members of other tribes nowadays because there are not enough young Garou of one tribe at the local septs to form packs. Plus they want an opportunity to earn Renown for themselves which is harder to do if a Cliath joins an established pack with lots of Adren or Fostern, or worse Athros or Elders. So young Garou of multiple tribes often join up and go Anruth visiting lots of different septs, doing jobs for them until they become Adren or so. Then the pack breaks up as individual members go back to their home septs and begin to take leadership positions.<br /> <br /> The tribal opinions mentioned in the tribebooks are just general opinions of the tribe members as a whole. There is always going to be some variety of opinion, and there can be many individual members of even whole septs of that tribe who have very different opinions, especially in regards to THAT specific sept over there. The Red Talons may not like the Children of Gaia in general for example, but there is nothing that says this specific Red Talon sept and that nearby Children of Gaia sept get along very well because of the shared history they have. Those Red Talons may not like other Children of Gaia, but that sept there which has helped them out for centuries and with whom they have long standing cooperation, yeah, they're OK.<br /> <br /> It's really a question of what kind of dynamic you want for your games when you design your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T13:54:14-07:00","id":1534306,"title":"","content":"There is a wide spectrum to these things of course and multiple layers of nuance. Different tribes can have different systems of organization and what the common opinion of the tribe, what the current stance of the tribe\u2019s leaders, the particular stance of the tribal members in certain septs, the opinions of the various tribal camps and factions, and of course individual tribe members often do not match up 1:1 with each other although they will usually be in a sort of communication.<br /> <br /> At the most broad level there are of course a few archetypal tribal conflicts which can occur. The Bone Gnawers may be the brunt of derision of other tribes although are usually tolerated if they stay (more or less in line), although I had one game where the PC Silent Strider Strider Theurge openly loathed our PC Bone Gnawer Ragabash. The Children of Gaia suffer from their poor writing and might be disparaged by others but I\u2019ve never seen it in play unless a PC intentionally makes their Coggie obnoxious (kind of like the old D&amp;D Paladin problem). Of course the Black Furies can have problems with tribes associated with patriarchal tendencies (high tribes, Fenrir, shadow lords, etc.) but this hasn\u2019t come up in play for me unless the players make it a story beat (like the game where an arrogant PC Fianna Ahroun &amp; PC Shadow Lord Philodox needed the PC Black Fury Ragabash to better understand the capabilities of female Garou and kinfolk; it was mostly a kinfolk issue tbh - the Fianna was over-protective and the Shadow Lord was over-exploitative). Fenrir can cause problems if they\u2019re played to the hilt as bruisers, especially with Coggies or any other PCs who prefer subtlety. Silver Fangs can be overbearing. Red Talons can make tension run high on the human-question and Younger Brother/Galestalkers in particular may have tension with the European high tribes), etc. <br /> <br /> Ultimately it\u2019s highly circumstantial but I definitely feel that these layers of tribal dynamics are important to portraying the setting and that both STs and players ought to give it some thought for their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T16:31:17-07:00","id":1534310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1534306#post1534306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a wide spectrum to these things of course and multiple layers of nuance. Different tribes can have different systems of organization and what the common opinion of the tribe, what the current stance of the tribe\u2019s leaders, the particular stance of the tribal members in certain septs, the opinions of the various tribal camps and factions, and of course individual tribe members often do not match up 1:1 with each other although they will usually be in a sort of communication.<br /> <br /> At the most broad level there are of course a few archetypal tribal conflicts which can occur. The Bone Gnawers may be the brunt of derision of other tribes although are usually tolerated if they stay (more or less in line), although I had one game where the PC Silent Strider Strider Theurge openly loathed our PC Bone Gnawer Ragabash. The Children of Gaia suffer from their poor writing and might be disparaged by others but I\u2019ve never seen it in play unless a PC intentionally makes their Coggie obnoxious (kind of like the old D&amp;D Paladin problem). Of course the Black Furies can have problems with tribes associated with patriarchal tendencies (high tribes, Fenrir, shadow lords, etc.) but this hasn\u2019t come up in play for me unless the players make it a story beat (like the game where an arrogant PC Fianna Ahroun &amp; PC Shadow Lord Philodox needed the PC Black Fury Ragabash to better understand the capabilities of female Garou and kinfolk; it was mostly a kinfolk issue tbh - the Fianna was over-protective and the Shadow Lord was over-exploitative). Fenrir can cause problems if they\u2019re played to the hilt as bruisers, especially with Coggies or any other PCs who prefer subtlety. Silver Fangs can be overbearing. Red Talons can make tension run high on the human-question and Younger Brother/Galestalkers in particular may have tension with the European high tribes), etc.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it\u2019s highly circumstantial but I definitely feel that these layers of tribal dynamics are important to portraying the setting and that both STs and players ought to give it some thought for their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very interesting point of view, but wouldn't that stall the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T23:02:25-07:00","id":1534323,"title":"","content":"Well I remember that in Minds eye theater version of WTA the garou nation is split between two tribal alliances:<br /> <br /> The Eastern and Western Concordat, which roughly maps to progressive and conservative the member tribes are, though to be clear that isn't a hard split like the camarilla and sabbat (or the forsaken and the pure), both alliances acknowledge that they on the same mission (to fight gaia's enemies, kill BSD's, ect) and both sides would rather to stay out of each other way then actually try to kill each other, since the split is mainly political rather then some ancient blood feud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-17-2024, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T03:46:39-07:00","id":1534327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1534310#post1534310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A very interesting point of view, but wouldn't that stall the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...that is the game. Finding a way to find common ground and try and come together as Family to fix issues is kinda what WtA is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T13:15:21-07:00","id":1534365,"title":"","content":"It could stall the game but it\u2019s one of those things that all the STs and players need to be on the same page about on a meta level, if people like it for the story and/or gameplay effects, then it\u2019s fine but if not then it\u2019s probably best just to shelf that element:\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T06:22:01-07:00","id":1534487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1534310#post1534310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A very interesting point of view, but wouldn't that stall the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because that is the whole point. A clash of viewpoints and philosophies, traditions and grudges - contrasted against the need to do something now and to work together for the greater good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T07:42:53-07:00","id":1534637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1534323#post1534323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I remember that in Minds eye theater version of WTA the garou nation is split between two tribal alliances:<br /> <br /> The Eastern and Western Concordat, which roughly maps to progressive and conservative the member tribes are, though to be clear that isn't a hard split like the camarilla and sabbat (or the forsaken and the pure), both alliances acknowledge that they on the same mission (to fight gaia's enemies, kill BSD's, ect) and both sides would rather to stay out of each other way then actually try to kill each other, since the split is mainly political rather then some ancient blood feud.</div> </div> </div> </div> This was, in truth, an excellent notion: we\u2019ve seen the tribes quarrel and even war with each other before, but I\u2019m not sure there\u2019s ever been a comparable situation in the backstory of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-27T04:44:11-07:00","id":1534801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1534637#post1534637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was, in truth, an excellent notion: we\u2019ve seen the tribes quarrel and even war with each other before, but I\u2019m not sure there\u2019s ever been a comparable situation in the backstory of the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the spilt actually happened relatively recently. Around the 1985 according to werewolf the essentials (which derive some amount of it's lore from the Minds eye Theater version) after some heavy shit happened and shook the garou nation to the core.<br /> <br /> Any way Here's a breakdown both the tribes alliances are split (Note that this from werewolf the essentials which while basing it's lore on Minds eye Theater: werewolf isn't a 1 to 1 copy of it.):<br /> <br /> The Eastern Concordat:<ul><li>Black Furies</li> <li>Bone Gnawers</li> <li>Children of Gaia (along with few camps of stargazers that joined up with them)</li> <li>Shadow Lords (surprisingly they're actually one of founders of the alliance)</li> </ul>The Western Concordat:<ul><li>Get of Fenris</li> <li>Silver Fangs</li> <li>Glass Walkers (tried to join up with the Eastern Concordat during the split but kinfolk rights was a hot button topic and most of the Eastern Concordat find the glass walkers lacking on that front...)</li> <li>Skysingers (renamed fenna)</li> </ul>Other/unaligned<ul><li>Red Talons (they aren't interested in the thing the humanoids call &quot;politics&quot;)</li> <li>Silent Striders (they search for new cereins after most of the old ones went ka-boom in the 80s)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-28-2024, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:40:40-07:00","id":1536357,"title":"","content":"I slightly dislike the name \u2018Skysingers\u2019 for the Fianna: there are already quite a lot of Tribes with \u2018S\u2019 names, so this particular rebranding just adds to the profusion (I\u2019m not enormously keen on \u2018Hart Wardens\u2019, but it avoids the \u2018S problem\u2019 at least).<br /> <br /> Also, may I please ask why Elder Brother and Younger Brother are not in the list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Needed to add a courtesy. 05-27-2024, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T00:52:28-07:00","id":1536411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1536357#post1536357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, may I please ask why Elder Brother and Younger Brother are not in the list?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm well both brothers (renamed Kalaril and Hapil ) seem to have sided to with the Dawn Tribes. Which is basically the North American version of the Beast Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":".  added more context 05-28-2024, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T07:51:28-07:00","id":1536428,"title":"","content":"It really does sound like MET and Paradox W:tA just wholly retreated the Avatar Storm of Mage Revised, but for Garou and Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T11:49:49-07:00","id":1536448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1536428#post1536428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really does sound like MET and Paradox W:tA just wholly retreated the Avatar Storm of Mage Revised, but for Garou and Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>They even retcon shoved Garou suffering injuries from the Avatar Storm into the hatchet job they did on Changing Ways........and of course continued it into W5....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T03:32:31-07:00","id":1536491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534297-eachothers-throat?p=1536428#post1536428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really does sound like MET and Paradox W:tA just wholly retreated the Avatar Storm of Mage Revised, but for Garou and Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now let's see what they do for Mage!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Mem